[178.481126, "o", "**Distance Control Complexity**: Desired distance is dynamic (10m + 1.5s × ego_speed). At 28 m/s cruise, desired distance is 52m. Sensor data shows actual distances of 35-40m, creating large steady-state errors.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[178.481155, "o", "> "]
[178.48143, "o", "**Steady-State Tracking**: Low integral gains prevent windup but limit steady-state error correction. Higher ki would improve tracking but increase overshoot and oscillation.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[178.481454, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[178.481567, "o", "## Recommendations\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[178.48163, "o", "1. **Anti-Windup**: Implement integral clamping and conditional integration\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[178.48168, "o", "> "]
[178.481784, "o", "2. **Advanced Control**: Consider Model Predictive Control for better lookahead\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[178.481867, "o", "3. **Adaptive Gains**: Speed-dependent gain scheduling\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[178.48192, "o", "> "]
[178.481963, "o", "4. **Mode Smoothing**: Bumpless transfer between modes\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[178.482008, "o", "> "]
[178.482102, "o", "5. **Distance Normalization**: Relative distance control instead of absolute\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[178.482127, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[178.482189, "o", "## Conclusion\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[178.482228, "o", "> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[178.48261, "o", "The ACC system provides functional cruise control with safe lead vehicle following and emergency braking. The rise time target is met, demonstrating responsive control. Further tuning and advanced control techniques would improve steady-state performance and reduce overshoot.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> EOF\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[178.483782, "o", "\u001b[?2004hroot@70733c13328d:~# "]
